# Repositories

Repositories encapsulate data access. The interface lives in `LoadlyAggregator.Domain/Common/Interfaces/IXRepository.cs`; the implementation lives here and inherits the generic `Repository<T>`.

## Rules

- `public class XRepository(ApplicationDbContext ctx) : Repository<X>(ctx), IXRepository`.
- Methods are **async** and return `Task` or `Task<...>`. Never `.Result`/`.Wait()`.
- Use `_dbSet` from the base class, not `_context.XTable`.
- Override `GetByIdAsync` only when you need Includes; otherwise the generic implementation is fine.
- Add use-case-specific finders here: `GetByUserNameAsync`, `GetByLoginAsync`, `GetWithContractsByCompanyIdAsync`, etc. — one method per read shape used by Actions.
- Normalize lookup values that are stored lowercased (email/username) at the repository boundary: `email.ToLower()`.
- Do **not** call `_unitOfWork.SaveChangesAsync()` in a repository. Writes stage changes; Actions commit via `IUnitOfWork`.
- Soft-delete filtering is applied automatically by the base; use `IncludeDeletedAsync(...)` or the explicit flag only when truly needed.
- No business rules, no translation, no `HttpContext`.

## Example (mirrors `AdminRepository`)

```csharp
public class AdminRepository(ApplicationDbContext ctx) : Repository<Admin>(ctx), IAdminRepository
{
    public override async Task<Admin?> GetByIdAsync(long id) =>
        await _dbSet
            .Where(a => a.Id == id)
            .Include(a => a.UserRoles.Where(r => r.ModelType == "Admin")).ThenInclude(ur => ur.Role)
            .FirstOrDefaultAsync();

    public async Task<Admin?> GetByEmailAsync(string email) =>
        await _dbSet.FirstOrDefaultAsync(a => a.Email == email.ToLower());
}
```

## Interface placement

New repository interfaces go in `LoadlyAggregator.Domain/Common/Interfaces/`. The Domain never references the Infrastructure implementation directly.

Register the new repo in `LoadlyAggregator.Infrastructure/Extensions/ServiceCollectionExtensions.cs` as `AddScoped<IXRepository, XRepository>()`.
